mdr sample document
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

This document covers every Markdown
element mdr supports. Run `mdr
examples/sample.md` to see it rendered.
Long paragraphs wrap to the terminal
width without ever splitting a word, and
line breaks inside a paragraph in the
source become ordinary spaces.

Inline styles
─────────────

Plain text, bold, italic, bold italic,
strikethrough, and inline code `cargo
build --release`. Styles can be nested:
bold with italic and `code`, or deleted
bold text.

This line ends with two spaces, which
forces a line break;
so this sentence starts on a new line.

Headings
────────

### Heading level 3

#### Heading level 4

##### Heading level 5

###### Heading level 6

Links and images
────────────────

• Link: The Rust website
  <https://www.rust-lang.org/>
• Autolink:
  https://github.com/pulldown-cmark/pull
  down-cmark
• Email link: mailto:hello@example.com
• Image: [image: a screenshot of mdr]
  <https://example.com/images/mdr-screen
  shot.png>

A local image in a paragraph of its own
is displayed inline in Ghostty and
kitty:

[image: a gradient demo image]
<demo.png>

Lists
─────

Unordered and nested:

• Fruit
  ◦ Apple
  ◦ Banana
    ▪ Lady Finger
    ▪ Cavendish
• Vegetables
• A deliberately long list item, to show
  that when an item runs past one line,
  the continuation lines align with the
  text of the first line instead of the
  left edge.

Ordered:

1. Install the Rust toolchain
2. Clone the repository and `cd` into it
3. Build it
   1. Debug: `cargo build`
   2. Release: `cargo build --release`
4. Run the tests

Task list:

[✓] Parse Markdown
[✓] Wrap wide characters
[ ] Footnotes
[ ] Configurable themes

Block quotes
────────────

│ Text in a block quote gets a bar on
│ its left. A quote can hold several
│ paragraphs, and long lines wrap to the
│ width just like everywhere else.
│
│ │ Quotes can be nested, and every
│ │ level gets its own bar.
│
│ • Quotes can contain lists
│ • and styles

│ Note
│ This is a GitHub-style alert.

│ Warning
│ Careful: never delete data without a
│ backup.

Code blocks
───────────

╭─ rust
│ use std::collections::HashMap;
│
│ /// Count how many times each word app
│ ↪ ears.
│ fn word_count(text: &str) -> HashMap<&
│ ↪ str, usize> {
│     let mut map = HashMap::new();
│     for word in text.split_whitespace(
│     ↪ ) {
│         *map.entry(word).or_insert(0) 
│         ↪ += 1;
│     }
│     map
│ }
╰─

╭─ python
│ def greet(name: str) -> str:
│     # Non-ASCII works too
│     return f"Hello, {name}! 你好！"
╰─

╭─ bash
│ cargo install --path .
│ cat README.md | mdr --width 60
╰─

╭─
│ A code block without a language is sho
│ ↪ wn as is, without highlighting.
╰─

Tables
──────

┌─────────┬─────────┬─────────┬────────┐
│ Element │ Syntax  │ Support │  Notes │
│         │         │   ed    │        │
├─────────┼─────────┼─────────┼────────┤
│ Heading │   `#`   │    ✓    │      6 │
│         │         │         │ levels │
├─────────┼─────────┼─────────┼────────┤
│ Bold    │ `**text │    ✓    │      — │
│         │   **`   │         │        │
├─────────┼─────────┼─────────┼────────┤
│ Table   │   GFM   │    ✓    │   auto │
│         │         │         │ widths │
├─────────┼─────────┼─────────┼────────┤
│ Footnot │ `[^1]`  │    ✗    │ planne │
│ e       │         │         │      d │
├─────────┼─────────┼─────────┼────────┤
│ Mixed   │  text   │    ✓    │   1234 │
│ 中文    │         │         │        │
└─────────┴─────────┴─────────┴────────┘

Cells that are too long wrap inside the
cell:

┌──────────────────┬───────────────────┐
│ Command          │ Description       │
├──────────────────┼───────────────────┤
│ `mdr file.md`    │ Render a Markdown │
│                  │ file; output      │
│                  │ longer than one   │
│                  │ screen is handed  │
│                  │ to the less pager │
├──────────────────┼───────────────────┤
│ `cat x.md | mdr` │ Read from         │
│                  │ standard input    │
├──────────────────┼───────────────────┤
│ `mdr --no-color` │ Turn off colors,  │
│                  │ handy for copying │
│                  │ plain text        │
└──────────────────┴───────────────────┘

Wide characters
───────────────

CJK characters take two columns each,
and wrapping and tables account for
that. 中文、日本語、한국어 mixed with
English wrap correctly at any width, and
punctuation such as 「，。」 never
starts a line. A line break between CJK
characters in the source doesn't turn
into a stray space: 这一句在源文件里被拆
成了两行，渲染后仍然是连续的。

┌────────┬─────────────────────────────┐
│ 语言   │ 示例                        │
├────────┼─────────────────────────────┤
│ 中文   │ 终端里的 Markdown 渲染器    │
├────────┼─────────────────────────────┤
│ 日本語 │ ターミナルで Markdown を表  │
│        │ 示                          │
└────────┴─────────────────────────────┘

